WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:22.894
"I still can't believe Mrs. Smith left her glasses in her bird feeder," Henry said.

2
00:00:22.895 --> 00:00:29.972
"I know." His cousin Maggie laughed. "She's lucky a bird didn't peck them."

3
00:00:29.973 --> 00:00:39.261
"No, she's lucky that The Lemonade Detectives were around to track them down for her," said Henry's friend Cole.

4
00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:43.155
The Lemonade Detectives had been in business all summer.

5
00:00:43.156 --> 00:00:45.812
They'd solved lots of cases.

6
00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:51.485
Some cases were pretty simple, like finding Mrs. Smith's lost glasses.

7
00:00:51.486 --> 00:00:53.668
Other cases were trickier.

8
00:00:53.669 --> 00:00:59.098
But so far The Lemonade Detectives had solved them all.

9
00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:01.783
"Here come some customers."

10
00:01:01.784 --> 00:01:05.812
Henry saw two teenage girls walking toward them.

11
00:01:05.813 --> 00:01:10.845
"I wonder whether they want to buy lemonade or hire us to solve a mystery."

12
00:01:10.846 --> 00:01:14.586
"It's a mystery to me!" Cole joked with a grin.

13
00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:17.924
"Not to me," Maggie said, smiling.

14
00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:23.287
"Ashley and Jill buy at least one cup of lemonade apiece almost every day!"

15
00:01:23.288 --> 00:01:27.188
Sure enough the older girls ordered two lemonades.

16
00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:32.476
While Maggie was pouring their drinks, Ashley took a piece of paper out of her pocket.

17
00:01:32.477 --> 00:01:36.350
"Are you guys busy next Saturday?" She held out the paper.

18
00:01:36.351 --> 00:01:40.597
"Because we're having a fundraiser for the Belltown High School soccer team."

19
00:01:40.598 --> 00:01:47.859
"Ugh!" Cole groaned. "Don't talk about school! It's still summer, remember?"

20
00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:51.384
"Only for a few more weeks," Henry said.

21
00:01:51.385 --> 00:01:57.477
Ashley laughed. "I know. That's why we're holding the fundraiser."

22
00:01:57.478 --> 00:01:58.943
Jill nodded.

23
00:01:58.944 --> 00:02:03.027
"We're raising money before school starts so we can get new uniforms."

24
00:02:03.028 --> 00:02:06.543
Henry looked at the paper. It said:

25
00:02:06.544 --> 00:02:09.516
BELLTOWN HIGH SCHOOL FUNDRAISER

26
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:14.834
Enjoy the end of summer with a bike ride through beautiful Belltown Park

27
00:02:14.835 --> 00:02:18.865
All profits used to support the girls' soccer team

28
00:02:18.866 --> 00:02:22.806
$10 per person, snacks provided

29
00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:28.063
Cole was reading over Henry's shoulder. "Wow. That sounds cool.

30
00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:30.734
I love biking on those trails."

31
00:02:30.735 --> 00:02:34.064
"You can keep the flyer," Ashley said.

32
00:02:34.065 --> 00:02:43.352
"If you decide to come, just bring your bike, a helmet, and ten dollars."

33
00:02:43.353 --> 00:02:48.604
Then she and Jill wandered off with their lemonade.

34
00:02:48.605 --> 00:02:54.187
Cole was still looking at the flyer. "We're going, right?" he said.

35
00:02:54.188 --> 00:02:57.037
"I'd like to do it," Henry said.

36
00:02:57.038 --> 00:03:00.700
"It sounds like fun, and it's for a good cause."

37
00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:04.319
"What about the lemonade stand?" Maggie asked.

38
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.213
"We probably won't have many customers that day anyway," Cole pointed out.

39
00:03:09.214 --> 00:03:11.536
"Lots of kids will be at the park."

40
00:03:11.537 --> 00:03:14.409
"Maybe you're right," Maggie said.

41
00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:17.971
"Besides we made lots of money this week.

42
00:03:17.972 --> 00:03:24.388
I guess we can donate some of it to a good cause."

43
00:03:24.389 --> 00:03:32.687
It was the day of the fundraiser.

44
00:03:32.688 --> 00:03:39.017
The Lemonade Detectives had just ridden their bikes into Belltown Park.

45
00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:47.062
"Wow. There are tons of people here!" Cole exclaimed.

46
00:03:47.063 --> 00:03:49.901
"It looks like we sign in over there."

47
00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:55.173
Maggie pointed to a table draped with Belltown High School's colors, blue and white.

48
00:03:55.174 --> 00:03:59.716
Ashley and Jill were sitting behind the table with some of their teammates.

49
00:03:59.717 --> 00:04:04.595
Henry walked over. "Hi. We're here to ride."

50
00:04:04.596 --> 00:04:09.273
"Great!" Jill smiled. "Ten dollars each, please."

51
00:04:09.274 --> 00:04:12.404
Henry and his friends handed over their money.

52
00:04:12.405 --> 00:04:15.697
In exchange, Jill handed each of them a ticket.

53
00:04:15.698 --> 00:04:19.057
"Make sure you don't lose those," she said.

54
00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:22.598
"Everyone who finishes the ride gets a T-shirt at the end."

55
00:04:22.599 --> 00:04:28.286
"Really?" Maggie looked surprised. "How can you afford that?

56
00:04:28.287 --> 00:04:31.091
I thought you were trying to raise money."

57
00:04:31.092 --> 00:04:34.550
Ashley heard her and looked over.

58
00:04:34.551 --> 00:04:39.153
"The T-shirts are being donated by Belltown Bikes," she said.

59
00:04:39.154 --> 00:04:41.466
"They're our sponsor."

60
00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.425
She pointed to a sign advertising the local bicycle shop.

61
00:04:45.426 --> 00:04:51.654
Meanwhile Henry heard someone calling his name. It was his friend Nathan.

62
00:04:51.655 --> 00:04:55.254
"Are you guys riding too?" Nathan asked.

63
00:04:55.255 --> 00:04:59.698
"Yeah," Cole said. "Just like everybody else in town!"

64
00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:04.123
"And some people from out of town too," Maggie added.

65
00:05:04.124 --> 00:05:07.306
"Look! Isn't that a Valley High T-shirt?"

66
00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:12.055
She pointed to a teenage boy wearing a red-and-gold Valley High shirt.

67
00:05:12.056 --> 00:05:15.585
Valley High was the high school in a neighboring town.

68
00:05:15.586 --> 00:05:18.365
Nathan pointed in a different direction.

69
00:05:18.366 --> 00:05:22.908
"That dark-haired girl Tina goes to Valley High too," he said.

70
00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:25.744
"She babysits my little sister sometimes."

71
00:05:25.745 --> 00:05:28.688
"That's weird," Cole said.

72
00:05:28.689 --> 00:05:33.046
"Why would people from Valley High want to raise money for Belltown?

73
00:05:33.047 --> 00:05:35.469
They're our biggest rivals!"

74
00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:39.144
"If you think that's weird, look at that guy."

75
00:05:39.145 --> 00:05:42.921
Maggie was staring at a man standing by himself.

76
00:05:42.922 --> 00:05:46.356
Most of the riders were kids or teenagers.

77
00:05:46.357 --> 00:05:50.413
The adults were mostly teachers or coaches from Belltown High.

78
00:05:50.414 --> 00:05:53.474
But Henry didn't recognize this man.

79
00:05:53.475 --> 00:05:58.778
He was in his twenties, with very broad shoulders and dark sunglasses.

80
00:05:58.779 --> 00:06:02.586
"Maybe he just likes bike riding," Henry said.

81
00:06:02.587 --> 00:06:06.235
"He doesn't look very happy to be here," Cole said.

82
00:06:06.236 --> 00:06:09.120
"He's not smiling or talking to anyone."

83
00:06:09.121 --> 00:06:12.403
Just then someone shouted for attention.

84
00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:16.717
It was Ms. Hernandez, the girls' soccer coach.

85
00:06:16.718 --> 00:06:20.708
"Is everyone ready to have some fun?" she called.

86
00:06:20.709 --> 00:06:32.582
That made Henry forget about everything else. The ride was about to start!
